<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
MoveIt semantics for the OpenArm right arm in fm_control's canonical openarm_* names,
for the sim-only Servo (launch/openarm_sim_servo.launch.py).

Pairs with openarm.sim.urdf.xacro built as robot_preset:=default_bimanual
emit_grasp_frame:=true, with either hand: the loader hand (the default) and the pinch
gripper name their TCP the same. The right_arm group is a chain from the body to that
grasp frame, so MoveIt's IK base (Servo's planning frame) is
openarm_body_link0 and the chain tip (Servo's end effector) is the fm_openarm_v2
profile's ee_frame. Only the seven revolute arm joints are active in the chain; the
fixed mount, hand and grasp-frame joints add no DOF.

There is no collision matrix, so this SRDF is not fit for a real arm: servo_sim.yaml
runs with collision checking off.
-->
<!-- Robot name matches openarm.sim.urdf.xacro; MoveIt rejects a mismatched pair. -->
<robot name="openarm_v20">
    <group name="right_arm">
        <chain base_link="openarm_body_link0" tip_link="openarm_right_grasp_frame"/>
    </group>
</robot>
